  "title": "Journal v2: schema-validated events, run index, and a replay digest",
  "summary": "The journal grows from a single append-only buffer file into a five-module subsystem. Events gain a typed envelope (actor, work item, change, cost), are validated against a JSON Schema before any byte is written, and are stored under `runs/` instead of `buffer/`. A per-work-item index records which runs belong to which work item under a file lock, and a reader replays a run, checking every hash link and refusing a partial chain. The chain hash still proves the journal is intact; a new replay digest covers only the decision fields, so two runs with identical decisions match even when timings, cache outcomes and run ids differ.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
